### Authoring or modifying a skill

**You own the voice of the rule.**

In this repo the artifact is usually a Cursor rule under `.cursor/rules/`. Always-on guidance sets `alwaysApply: true` and stays short. A workflow that should load only when relevant sets `alwaysApply: false` and puts the trigger in `description`. A skill under `.cursor/skills/` or `.claude/skills/` follows the same shape when the user asked for a skill file.

1. Author or edit the file. Front-load trigger branches in `description`. Body is ordered steps, each ending in a completion criterion. Name host tools the way `.cursor/rules/rigor-mode.mdc` does (Task, Read, verify on the real surface). Do not require a plugin slash command or a subagent type this host does not have. Done when the file exists with frontmatter and every step has a criterion.
2. Validate. Referenced files exist. Cross-rule links resolve. No inlined tool schema. Done when validation notes list zero broken links.
3. Test cases if the change is structural. Skip if subjective. Done when tests ran or `skip: subjective` is on the todo.
4. Run Opening a PR (`.cursor/rules/rigor-playbook-opening-a-pr.mdc`). Done when the PR URL exists.

When in doubt, delete. Keep only prose that changes a decision. Point at structural sources (types, READMEs, config). Delegate to another rule by path. A workflow you keep hitting that is not captured becomes a new agent-requested rule.

**Reply:** summary of the rule, key design decisions, validation notes.
